  "title": "'Copy Link' menu option gives wrong link.",
  "content": "<p>I have copied this link from the post “STM32CubeIDE 2.2.0 released”:</p><p><a href=\"https://community.st.com/stm32cubeide-mcus-28/stm32cubeide-2-2-0-released-166532?postid=166532#post166532\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_self\">https://community.st.com/stm32cubeide%2Dmcus%2D28/stm32cubeide%2D2%2D2%2D0%2Dreleased%2D166532?postid=166532#post166532</a></p><p> </p><p>But that link actually goes to:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-embedded-software-32/how-to-send-int-values-efficiently-through-cdc-usb-39682?postid=166532#post166532\"></oembed><p>Text of the URL (with the https prefix removed, to stop the forum linkifying it):</p><p>community.st.com/stm32-mcus-embedded-software-32/how-to-send-int-values-efficiently-through-cdc-usb-39682?postid=166532#post166532</p><p>Which does, in fact have the same <code>?postid=166532#post166532</code> as the other link!</p>",
